{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The simulator supports the atoms enumerated by "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MM4\/documentation\/MM4\/MM4AtomCode"},{"type":"text","text":", with some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restrictions on permitted bond types. Elements except C, Si, Ge must have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every covalent bond shared with a carbon atom. In addition, no dissimilar"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"non-H\/C atoms may be separated by a bond once removed. Within these"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restrictions, there exists a large variety of permissible structures, more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than with exclusively carbon and hydrogen."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All force terms from MM3, and most terms from MM4, are included, except:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Electronegativity effect correction to equilibrium bond angle"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Electronegativity effect correction to bond stretching stiffness"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Torsion-torsion interaction","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Bend-torsion-bend interaction in bulk diamond","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The simulator uses 32-bit single precision and an NVE ensemble. Single"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"precision is often associated with poor energy conservation. However, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reason for using NVE is not energy conservation. The default time step is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so large that integration error dwarfs rounding error. Switching to 64-bit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"double precision would not improve energy conservation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Accuracy (whether an archer hits the right target) is orthogonal","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to precision (whether the arrows hit the same place every time).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Conservation of energy only affects the number of significant figures of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measured energy (precision). It does not make system dynamics more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accurate, except in the case where energy systematically drifts upward.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Single precision is an implementation choice to make the simulator more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compatible with different GPU architectures. Most vendors have no or few","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"FP64 units (unlike CPU, where FP64 is widely supported). Mixed precision","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can sometimes run the bulk of computations in FP32, with only the energy","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"computations in FP64. However, even mixed precision has implementation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"issues, being difficult to run on GPUs with zero FP64 units.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MM4\/documentation\/MM4","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/mm4"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"MM4","symbolKind":"module","tit